{"id": "EUVD-2026-93203", "enisaUuid": "713dcc1c-6d84-319c-8794-f5bcb6e6d813", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ethernet: cortina: Ack RX overrun interrupt correctly\n\nThe RX overrun interrupt is reported in interrupt status register 4, but\ngmac_irq() acknowledges it using the RX descriptor error bit from status\nregister 0. For GMAC0 this writes the GMAC1 overrun bit, while for GMAC1\nthe shift leaves no bit in the 32-bit register.\n\nAcknowledge the same per-port RX overrun bit that was detected.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1163cc82dcbc145f912bf2106ab668762f53e483", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12a0c7bb448c1899ea3d8f97fa47a8740044e16d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d72d87926ca33c6766dc73ace46859d7220a45bb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/472493d1d3334d104b9873abc1c2d80ed3b144f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f23fa11fef9b4a93335894379d82238f0a28228", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f33e036e827f368cdb10bcb15ad098448aca0f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4bd670454390aab72ab9fb7b73bce2966c33fe3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1dd85662fee6e2ac580b1c4f9a0c0a7ae6e31f0e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pxvw-xq3p-q24h", "CVE-2026-98275"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13194808-f5db-360d-9e3e-42d613b5e21b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4d5ae32f5e1e13f7f36d6439ec3257993b9f5b88 <d72d87926ca33c6766dc73ace46859d7220a45bb"}, {"id": "19f80912-68b6-3f37-ad2d-1b756df0f451", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "1e55dbf7-7a2d-33c9-8e31-ec2897245193", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "1f9fcfa3-d789-3ebe-921f-07db1ed211d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}},